---
import CalcPage from '../components/CalcPage.astro';
import def, { PITCHES } from '../calculators/shingle';
import { pitchFactor } from '../lib/finish';
import { fmt, ceilCount } from '../lib/format';

const pitches = PITCHES.map((p) => ({ p, f: pitchFactor(p), deg: (Math.atan(p / 12) * 180) / Math.PI }));
const houses = [1000, 1500, 2000, 2500, 3000].map((a) => {
  const sq = (a * pitchFactor(6) * 1.1) / 100;
  return { a, sq, bundles: ceilCount(sq * 3) };
});
---

<CalcPage
  slug="shingle-calculator"
  def={def}
  title="Shingle Calculator: Roofing Squares & Bundles by Pitch"
  description="Free roofing shingle calculator. Enter the roof footprint and pitch to get the sloped roof area, squares, and bundles of shingles, with waste for hips and valleys."
  h1="Shingle Calculator"
  updated="2026-09-26"
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    Find how many squares and bundles of shingles your roof needs. Measure the footprint from below, pick the pitch, and
    the calculator works out the sloped area.
  </Fragment>

  <h2 id="how-to">How to calculate roofing shingles</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Measure the roof's footprint: the length and width of the house plus the overhangs.</li>
    <li>Multiply by the pitch factor to convert that flat area to the actual sloped roof area.</li>
    <li>Add 10% for a simple gable roof, 15% for hips and valleys.</li>
    <li>Divide by 100 for squares, and multiply by 3 bundles per square for most shingles.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="example">Example: a 50 × 30 ft roof at 6/12 pitch</h2>
  <p>
    The footprint is 1,500 square feet. At 6/12 the pitch factor is 1.118, so the roof is 1,677 square feet. With 10%
    waste that is 1,845 square feet, or 18.45 squares. At 3 bundles per square you need <strong>56 bundles</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="pitch">Roof pitch factors</h2>
  <p>Multiply the flat footprint by the factor to get the sloped area.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Pitch</th><th class="num">Angle</th><th class="num">Factor</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{pitches.map((r) => <tr><td>{r.p}/12</td><td class="num">{fmt(r.deg, 1)}°</td><td class="num">{fmt(r.f, 3)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="table">Shingles by roof footprint</h2>
  <p>6/12 pitch, 10% waste, 3 bundles per square.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Footprint</th><th class="num">Squares</th><th class="num">Bundles</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{houses.map((h) => <tr><td>{h.a.toLocaleString('en-US')} sq ft</td><td class="num">{fmt(h.sq, 1)}</td><td class="num">{h.bundles}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Framing the roof as well? <a href="/rafter-calculator/">Find the rafter length</a> from the same span and pitch.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <h3>How many bundles of shingles are in a square?</h3>
  <p>
    Three for most architectural and 3-tab shingles, each bundle covering about 33.3 square feet. Some heavier or premium
    shingles take four. The wrapper states the coverage.
  </p>
  <h3>How do I find my roof pitch?</h3>
  <p>
    Hold a level horizontally against the roof or a rafter, measure 12 inches along it, and measure straight up to the
    roof surface. That rise in inches is the pitch: 6 inches means 6/12.
  </p>
  <h3>What else do I need besides shingles?</h3>
  <p>
    Underlayment, starter strip along the eaves, ridge cap for hips and ridges, drip edge, flashing, and roofing nails.
    Starter and ridge cap are ordered by the linear foot.
  </p>
  <p>Residing the walls as well? The <a href="/siding-calculator/">siding calculator</a> also works in squares.</p>

  <h2 id="method">How this calculator works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pitch factor = √(1 + (rise ÷ 12)²).</li>
    <li>Sloped area = footprint × pitch factor; squares = area × (1 + waste %) ÷ 100.</li>
    <li>Bundles = squares × bundles per square, rounded up. The roof is assumed to have one pitch throughout.</li>
  </ul>
</CalcPage>
